e squirrel likes the cow and the squirrel is not green, then the squirrel needs the rabbit.\n16.If something needs the squirrel, then the squirrel needs the cow.\n\nNow, the question is about the rabbit\'s roughness.The statement to evaluate is "The rabbit is not rough."So, I need to determine if this is true, false, or unknown based on the given information.But wait, let me make sure I\'m not missing anything.Maybe there\'s a reason why it\'s not necessarily true.Let me check if there\'s any information that contradicts this. So, unless there\'s a rule that affects the rabbit\'s roughness indirectly, it should hold.Let me see if any other statements imply the rabbit\'s roughness. Again, this is about the squirrel needing the rabbit, not the rabbit\'s roughness.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
