 if he\'s big yet.So this doesn\'t directly tell us about Dave\'s size.\n\nFact 16 says that if Dave is not cold, then he is not red.Since Dave is not cold (fact 4), according to fact 16, he must not be red.So Dave is not red.\n\nWait, but the question is asking if Dave is not red.If Dave is not red, then the statement "Dave is not red" would be true.So the answer would be A) True.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.Let\'s see:.\n\n- Dave is not cold (fact 4).\n- Fact 16: If Dave is not cold, then he is not red.So yes, Dave is not red\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
