nsparent or something, but in this context, I don\'t think that\'s considered.So, perhaps Bob is either red or not red, but not both.\n\nLooking at fact 14: If Bob is white, then Bob is furry.But from fact 2, Bob is red, so the condition "Bob is white" is false.In logic, if the antecedent of an implication is false, the implication is automatically true, regardless of the consequent.So, fact 14 doesn\'t give us any new information because Bob isn\'t white.Bob is definitely not red because he\'s white.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
