messages:   18%|#8        | 109/600 [15:53<12:40,  1.55s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is rough. Dave is blue. Dave is cold. Dave is red. Dave is rough. Dave is round. Gary is round. Harry is cold. Harry is rough. All round things are blue. If something is cold then it is blue. Blue, red things are round. If something is rough then it is red. All big, red things are cold. All round things are green. Round, cold things are big. If something is green then it is blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Dave is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is rough.\n3.Dave is blue.\n4.Dave is cold.\n5.Dave is red.\n6.Dave is rough.\n7.Dave is round.\n8.Gary is round.\n9.Harry is cold.\n10.Harry is rough.\n11.All round things are blue.\n12.If something is cold, then it is blue.\n13.Blue, red things are round.\n14.If something is rough, then it is red.\n15.All big, red things are cold.\n16.All round things are green.\n17.Round, cold things are big.\n18.If something is green, then it is blue.\n\nNow, I need to see if "Dave is big" can be determined from these statements.\n\nStarting with Dave\'s properties:.\n\n- Dave is blue (statement 3).\n- Dave is cold (statement 4).\n- Dave is red (statement 5).\n- Dave is rough (statement 6).\n- Dave is round (statement 7).\n\nWait, that\'s a problem.If Dave is both blue and red, that seems contradictory because typically, something can\'t be both blue and red unless specified otherwise.But the context doesn\'t mention anything about things being both colors.So maybe it\'s allowed, but I\'ll keep that in mind.\n\nNext, looking at the rules:.\n\nRule 11: All round things are blue.So anything that\'s round must be blue.Dave is round (statement 7), so that fits because rule 11 says round things are blue, and Dave is blue.So that\'s consistent.\n\nRule 12: If something is cold, then it is blue.Dave is cold (statement 4), so according to rule 12, it should be blue, which it is.So that\'s consistent too.\n\nRule 13: Blue, red things are round.So anything that\'s either blue or red must be round.Dave is both blue and red, so he must be round, which he is.So that\'s consistent.\n\nRule 14: If something is rough, then it is red.Dave is rough (statement 6), so he should be red, which he is.So that\'s consistent.\n\nRule 15: All big, red things are cold.So if something is big and red, it must be cold.But Dave is red, but we don\'t know if he\'s big yet.So this rule doesn\'t directly tell us about Dave\'s size.\n\nRule 16: All round things are green.Wait, Dave is round (statement 7), so according to rule 16, he should be green.But statement 3 says Dave is blue.So that\'s a contradiction.Because rule 16 says round things are green, but Dave is round and blue.That can\'t be both.\nDave is not big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
