t big and not blue, or not big and blue.\n\nBut we don't have any information that definitively says he's not big.\n\nWait, but let's think about the other characters again.\n\nFiona is big and blue.\n\nHarry is blue, round, and smart.\n\nGary is white and round.\n\nSo, if Charlie were big, he would have to be not blue, but we don't know.\n\nBut from fact 15, if he's round, he's big, but we don't know if he's round.\n\nAlternatively, if he's not big, he's not round.\n\nBut without any information about Charlie's size or color, we can't determine for sure.\n\nWait, but let's think about fact 12: Young, white things are round.\n\nSo, if Charlie were white and young, he'd be round, but we don't know if he's white.\n\nBut if he's white, he's round, and then from fact 15, he's big.\n\nBut if he's white and round, he's big, but then from fact 8, if he's big and quiet, he's not smart, but we don't know if he's smart.\n\nBut this is getting too convoluted.\n\nI think the key is that from fact 15, round things are big, so if Charlie is round, he's big, but if he's big, he can't be round because that would make him quiet, which would make him not young, but he is young.\n\nWait, no, if he's round and quiet, he's not young, but he is young, so he can't be round and quiet, but he could be round and not quiet, making him big.\n\nBut we don't know if he's quiet or not.\n\nAlternatively, if he's not round, he's not big.\n\nBut we don't know if he's round.\n\nSo, without information about Charlie's roundness, we can't determine if he's big or not.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Charlie is not big\" is unknown.\n\nWait, but that can't be right because from fact 15, if he's round, he's big, but if he's not round, he's not big.\n\nBut we don't know if he's round.\n\nSo, the answer is unknown.\n\nWait, but let me check again.\n\nIf Charlie is big, then he's not blue (from fact 11), but we don't know if he's blue.\n\nIf he's not big, he's not round (from fact 15), but we don't know if he