e bald eagle, then the rabbit visits the bald eagle.\n17.If something is rough, then it visits the lion.\n18.If the dog needs the rabbit and the rabbit sees the bald eagle, then the bald eagle sees the dog.\n19.If the rabbit visits the lion and the rabbit needs the dog, then the dog is round.\n20.If something visits the rabbit, then the rabbit needs the bald eagle.\n21.If something visits the lion and the lion needs the dog, then it needs the dog.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the bald eagle does not need the lion.From statement 3, it says "The bald eagle needs the lion."So, according to the given information, the bald eagle does need the lion.Therefore, the statement "The bald eagle does not need the lion" would be false.I believe I have simplified it.  The crucial point is statement 3: The lion does not need the bald eagle.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
