 (18).\n\n- The cow dislikes the rabbit (18).\n\nWait, that's a contradiction.\n\nWait, no, statement 18 says if something is blue, then it likes the rabbit.\n\nSo, the cow is blue (12), so it likes the rabbit (18).\n\nBut statement 13 says if something likes the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow, then the cow is young.\n\nBut the cow likes the rabbit, but does the rabbit visit the cow?\n\nFrom statement 15: If something is round and it sees the cow, then the cow sees the rabbit.\n\nThe bald eagle is round (14) and sees the cow (16), so the cow sees the rabbit (15).\n\nSo, the cow sees the rabbit.\n\nTherefore, the cow likes the rabbit (18) and the rabbit sees the cow (15).\n\nSo, statement 13 says if the cow likes the rabbit and the rabbit visits the cow, then the cow is young.\n\nBut we know the cow likes the rabbit, but do we know if the rabbit visits the cow?\n\nStatement 15 says that if the bald eagle sees the cow, then the cow sees the rabbit.\n\nBut the rabbit visiting the cow is a separate statement.\n\nWait, statement 13 is about the rabbit visiting the cow, not the cow seeing the rabbit.\n\nSo, the cow sees the rabbit (15), but the rabbit may or may not visit the cow.\n\nTherefore, we don't know if the rabbit visits the cow, so we can't apply statement 13.\n\nTherefore, the cow's age is unknown.\n\nSo, the answer is C) Unknown.\n</think>\n\nThe cow's age cannot be determined from the given statements. \n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. The cow is blue (12) because it likes the bald eagle (2).\n2. The cow likes the rabbit (18) because it's blue.\n3. The cow dislikes the rabbit (18) because it's blue.\n4. The cow sees the rabbit (15) because the bald eagle is round and sees the cow.\n5. The rabbit may or may not visit the cow, which is unknown.\n6. Without knowing if the rabbit visits the cow, we can't apply statement 13 to determine the cow's age.\n\nAnswer: C) Unknown",
