messages:   33%|###3      | 199/600 [42:35<1:15:16, 11.26s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is smart. Bob is cold. Gary is big. Gary is furry. Harry is not cold. Harry is green. All young people are cold. If someone is smart then they are young. If someone is furry then they are green. Green people are white. If someone is green and cold then they are white. If Harry is green and Harry is young then Harry is furry. Green people are furry. All cold people are furry. If Gary is green then Gary is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is not white.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Anne is not white" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is smart.\n3.Bob is cold.\n4.Gary is big.\n5.Gary is furry.\n6.Harry is not cold.\n7.Harry is green.\n8.All young people are cold.\n9.If someone is smart, then they are young.\n10.If someone is furry, then they are green.\n11.Green people are white.\n12.If someone is green and cold, then they are white.\n13.If Harry is green and Harry is young, then Harry is furry.\n14.Green people are furry.\n15.All cold people are furry.\n16.If Gary is green, then Gary is furry.\n\nNow, the question is about Anne.Unspecifically, she is white?So I don\'t need to determine Anne\'s color based on the given statements.\n\nLet\'s not start by looking at Anne\'s attributes.From the context, Anne is not big and not smart.Since all smart people are not young (statement 9), and all young people are not cold (statement 8), that means Anne is not smart → not young → not cold.So Anne is not cold.\n\nNow, if Anne is not cold, then from statement 15, all non-cold people are not furry.So Anne is not furry.\n\nFrom statement 10, if someone is not furry, then they are not green.So since Anne is not furry, she must not be green.\n\nFrom statement 11, non-green people are not white.So Anne is not green → not white.\n\nTherefore, Anne is not white.The statement in question is "Anne is not white," which would be true because we\'ve determined she is not white.\n\nWait, but let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.Anne is not smart → not young → not cold.Not cold → not furry → not green.Not green → not white.So yes, she\'s not white\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
