messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe bald eagle chases the rabbit. The bald eagle does not chase the tiger. The bald eagle is green. The bald eagle is red. The bald eagle is young. The bald eagle sees the rabbit. The bear sees the bald eagle. The rabbit is red. The rabbit needs the bald eagle. The tiger chases the bear. The tiger is green. The tiger sees the bald eagle. If something is young and red then it is green. If something sees the bear then it needs the tiger. If something needs the bald eagle then the bald eagle chases the rabbit. If something is big and it chases the rabbit then it sees the bear. If something sees the rabbit and it needs the tiger then the tiger is not blue. If something chases the rabbit then it sees the bald eagle. If the rabbit is not young and the rabbit does not need the bald eagle then the rabbit sees the bear. If something is red and it needs the bear then it is big. If something is red then it needs the bear.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The rabbit is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "The rabbit is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given logical context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the given statements to make it easier to reference:.\n\n1.The bald eagle chases the rabbit.\n2.The bald eagle does not chase the tiger.\n3.The bald eagle is green.\n4.The bald eagle is red.\n5.The bald eagle is young.\n6.The bear sees the bald eagle.\n7.The rabbit is red.\n8.The rabbit needs the bald eagle.\n9.The tiger chases the bear.\n10.The tiger is green.\n11.The tiger sees the bald eagle.\n12.If something is young and red then it is green.\n13.If something sees the bear then it needs the tiger.\n14.If something needs the bald eagle then the bald eagle chases the rabbit.\n15.If something is big and it chases the rabbit then it sees the bear.\n16.If something sees the rabbit and it needs the tiger then the tiger is not blue.\n17.If something chases the rabbit then it sees the bald eagle.\n18.If the rabbit is not young and the rabbit does not need the bald eagle then the rabbit sees the bear.\n19.If something is red and it needs the bear then it is big.\n20.If something is red then it needs the bear.\n\nNow, I need to determine if the rabbit is not big.So, I\'m looking to see if the rabbit is big or not.Let\'s see what we can deduce.\n\nFrom statement 7, the rabbit is red.From statement 19, if something is red and needs the bear, then it\'s big.So, if the rabbit is red and needs the bear, then it\'s big.But from statement 8, the rabbit needs the bald eagle.From statement 14, if something needs the bald eagle, then the bald eagle chases the rabbit.But statement 1 confirms that the bald eagle does chase the rabbit, so that\'s consistent.\n\nNow, looking at statement 18: If the rabbit is not young and does not need the bald eagle, then it sees the bear.But the rabbit does need the bald eagle (statement 8), so the condition for statement 18 is not met.Therefore, statement 18 doesn\'t tell us anything about the rabbit seeing the bear in this case.\n\nFrom statement 19, since the rabbit is red, if it needs the bear, then it\'s big.But does the rabbit need the bear?Statement 18 says that if the rabbit is not young and doesn\'t need the bald eagle, it sees the bear.But since the rabbit does need the bald eagle, it doesn\'t fall into that condition.So, we don\'t know if the rabbit sees the bear or not.\n\nLooking at statement 13: If something sees the bear, then it needs the tiger.The bear sees the bald eagle (statement 6), so the bear needs the tiger (from statement 13).The tiger is green (statement 10) and sees the bald eagle (statement 11).The tiger chases the bear (statement 9), so that\'s consistent.\n\nThe rabbit is big if it needs the bear, but we have enough information to confirm that. Alternatively, if the rabbit doesn\'t need the bear, it might be big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 40%|###9      | 237/600 [44:22<07:20,  1.21s/it]
