ng needs the cow and it is cold, then it is young.\n19.If something is nice, it visits the lion.\n20.If something needs the lion, it likes the cat.\n21.If something visits the cat and it likes the lion, the cat is blue.\n22.If something is cold and blue, it needs the lion.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the mouse needs the mouse.So, I need to see if there\'s any rule or statement that directly or indirectly leads to the mouse needing itself.\nThe mouse does not need the mouse, but it needs the cat and the cow.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
