se the reverse isn\'t stated.Just because something is green doesn\'t mean it\'s round.So we can\'t conclude that Anne is round from this.\n\nPoint 16 says that rough, nice things are quiet.But we don\'t know if Anne is rough or nice yet.Let\'s look at the other points.\n\nPoint 14 says all nice things are blue.So if something is nice, it must be blue.But we don\'t know if Anne is nice yet.\n\nPoint 5 says Fiona is not nice, and from point 6, Fiona is quiet.So Fiona is quiet and not nice.Point 16 says that rough, nice things are quiet, but since Fiona is quiet and not nice, that doesn\'t affect her because she\'s not nice.So Fiona being quiet doesn\'t make her nice or not, but she\'s definitely not nice.Based on the information provided, it\'s clear that Anne is not nice.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
