messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe bald eagle eats the bear. The bald eagle is nice. The bald eagle visits the mouse. The bear eats the tiger. The bear is kind. The bear visits the tiger. The mouse eats the bear. The mouse is green. The mouse is kind. The mouse sees the bald eagle. The mouse sees the bear. The mouse sees the tiger. The tiger eats the mouse. The tiger sees the bald eagle. The tiger sees the bear. The tiger visits the mouse. If something is kind then it visits the bald eagle. If something eats the bear then the bear sees the bald eagle. If the bald eagle is round then the bald eagle eats the bear. If something eats the bald eagle and it sees the bear then the bald eagle is kind. If something sees the bald eagle then the bald eagle visits the mouse. If something visits the bald eagle and the bald eagle visits the mouse then it eats the bald eagle. If something is blue and it eats the tiger then the tiger eats the mouse.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The bald eagle is not green.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "The bald eagle is not green" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the given statements to make it clearer:.\n\n1.The bald eagle eats the bear.\n2.The bald eagle is nice.\n3.The bald eagle visits the mouse.\n4.The bear eats the tiger.\n5.The bear is kind.\n6.The bear visits the tiger.\n7.The mouse eats the bear.\n8.The mouse is green.\n9.The mouse is kind.\n10.The mouse sees the bald eagle.\n11.The mouse sees the bear.\n12.The mouse sees the tiger.\n13.The tiger eats the mouse.\n14.The tiger sees the bald eagle.\n15.The tiger sees the bear.\n16.The tiger visits the mouse.\n17.If something is kind, then it visits the bald eagle.\n18.If something eats the bear, then the bear sees the bald eagle.\n19.If the bald eagle is round, then the bald eagle eats the bear.\n20.If something eats the bald eagle and it sees the bear, then the bald eagle is kind.\n21.If something sees the bald eagle, then the bald eagle visits the mouse.\n22.If something visits the bald eagle and the bald eagle visits the mouse, then it eats the bald eagle.\n23.If something is blue and it eats the tiger, then the tiger eats the mouse.\n\nNow, the question is about the color of the bald eagle.Specifically, is it not green?The options are A) True, B) False, C) Unknown.\n\nLooking at the given statements, I see that the mouse is green (statement 8).The bald eagle visits the mouse (statement 3).There\'s a rule that if something is kind, it visits the bald eagle (statement 17).The mouse is kind (statement 9), so according to statement 17, the mouse should visit the bald eagle.Indeed, statement 10 says the mouse sees the bald eagle, which aligns with that.\n\nNow, the bald eagle is nice (statement 2).The bear is kind (statement 5), and the bear visits the tiger (statement 6).The tiger eats the mouse (statement 13), and the mouse is green (statement 8).The mouse is also kind (statement 9), so the mouse visits the bald eagle (statement 10)..\n\nLooking at statement 20: If something eats the bald eagle and sees the bear, then the bald eagle is kind.But I don\'t see any statement where the bald eagle is eaten by something.The only predator mentioned is the bear (statement 4), but the bear doesn\'t eat the bald eagle; the bear eats the tiger (statement 4).So, the bear doesn\'t eat the bald eagle, so statement 20 doesn\'t apply here.\nThe bald eagle eats the bear, visits the mouse, and is eaten by the mouse if it is round, which doesn\'t provide any information about its color. Additionally, if something visits the bald eagle and the bald eagle visits the mouse, then that something would eat the bald eagle, creating a contradictory situation. Despite various statements, there is uncertainty about the bald eagle\'s color, with the only direct mention being the green mouse, leaving the bald eagle\'s color undetermined.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 41%|####1     | 247/600 [44:50<20:25,  3.47s/it]
