messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nCharlie is young. Erin is blue. Erin is not kind. Fiona is blue. Fiona is white. Gary is blue. Gary is kind. Furry, nice things are white. If something is young and blue then it is smart. All blue, smart things are furry. All smart, white things are furry. Young things are nice. If Fiona is smart and Fiona is young then Fiona is not furry. If Erin is kind then Erin is furry. If Gary is smart and Gary is white then Gary is not kind. If something is nice then it is blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is not white.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Fiona is not white" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Charlie is young.\n2.Erin is blue.\n3.Erin is not kind.\n4.Fiona is blue.\n5.Fiona is white.\n6.Gary is blue.\n7.Gary is kind.\n8.Furry, nice things are white.\n9.If something is young and blue, then it is smart.\n10.All blue, smart things are furry.\n11.All smart, white things are furry.\n12.Young things are nice.\n13.If Fiona is smart and Fiona is young, then Fiona is not furry.\n14.If Erin is kind, then Erin is furry.\n15.If Gary is smart and Gary is white, then Gary is not kind.\n16.If something is nice, it is blue.\n\nNow, the question is about Fiona\'s color.Specifically, is Fiona not white?So, I need to determine if "Fiona is not white" is true, false, or unknown.\n\nLooking at the facts, point 5 says Fiona is blue, and point 4 says Fiona is blue.Wait, that\'s a bit confusing because point 5 says Fiona is white, and point 4 says she\'s blue.Wait, no, let me check again.\n\nWait, point 4 says Erin is blue, and point 5 says Fiona is blue.But