ays all blue people are big.So, if Anne is blue, she must be big.\n\nBut let me check if there\'s any information about Anne\'s smartness.The facts don\'t mention anything about Anne\'s color, size, or smartness directly.The only people mentioned are Bob, Dave, and Fiona.\n\nLooking at the implications, fact 19 says that round, smart people are blue.So, if someone is both round and smart, they must be blue.But Anne is round, but we don\'t know if she\'s smart.If she were smart, then according to fact 19, she would have to be blue.But we don\'t have any information about Anne\'s color beyond being round, which would make her blue if she\'s smart.\n\nWait, but fact 15 says all round people are blue, so Anne is blue regardless of her smartness.But fact 19 adds that if someone is both round and smart, they are blue.But that doesn\'t necessarily mean that all blue people are smart, only that if they\'re smart and round, they are blue.\nAnne is not smart.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
