messages:   44%|####4     | 264/600 [49:46<13:08,  2.35s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is big. Bob is blue. Bob is cold. Bob is quiet. Bob is rough. Bob is smart. Bob is white. Dave is rough. Fiona is blue. Harry is big. Harry is cold. If someone is blue then they are cold. If someone is big then they are white. If Bob is rough and Bob is blue then Bob is big. All blue, smart people are big. If someone is blue and rough then they are quiet. All smart people are blue. Cold people are rough. If someone is quiet then they are big.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out whether Fiona is big based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Bob is big.\n2.Bob is blue.\n3.Bob is cold.\n4.Bob is quiet.\n5.Bob is rough.\n6.Bob is smart.\n7.Bob is white.Wait, that's interesting because Bob is both blue and white?That seems contradictory.Maybe it's a typo, but I'll proceed as is.\n8.Dave is rough.\n9.Fiona is blue.\n10.Harry is big.\n11.Harry is cold.\n12.If someone is blue, then they are cold.\n13.If someone is big, then they are white.\n14.If Bob is rough and blue, then Bob is big.But wait, Bob is already big, so this might be redundant or just confirming.\n15.All blue, smart people are big.So, if someone is both blue and smart, they must be big.\n16.If someone is blue and rough, then they are quiet.\n17.All smart people are blue.\n18.Cold people are rough.\n19.If someone is quiet, then they are big.\n\nNow, the question is: Is Fiona big?.\n\nLet's break it down.\n\nFrom point 9, Fiona is blue.So, Fiona is not blue.\n\nFrom point 12, if someone is not blue, they are not cold.So, Fiona is not cold.\n\nFrom point 18, not cold people are not rough.So, Fiona is not rough.\n\nFrom point 16, if someone is not blue or rough, then they are not quiet.So, Fiona is not quiet.\n\nFrom point 19, if someone is not quiet, then they are not big.So, Fiona is not big.\n\nWait, that seems to chain together.Let me check each step again.\n\n1.Fiona is not blue (given).\n2.Since all not blue people are not cold (point 12), Fiona is not cold.\n3.All not cold people are not rough (point 18), so Fiona is not rough.\n4.If someone is not blue or rough, they are not quiet (point 16).Since Fiona is neither blue nor rough, she is not quiet.\n5.If someone is not quiet, they are not big (point 19).Therefore, Fiona is not big.\n\nSo, based on these logical steps, Fiona must not be big\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
