messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is furry. Anne is nice. Anne is rough. Anne is white. Erin is furry. Erin is rough. Erin is white. Fiona is big. Fiona is nice. Fiona is round. Harry is nice. Harry is rough. All furry things are white. If Harry is red then Harry is round. All round, red things are furry. If Harry is rough then Harry is round. Nice, red things are big. Round, red things are white. All nice, white things are red. If something is round then it is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Harry is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Harry is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Anne is furry, nice, rough, and white.\n2.Erin is furry, rough, and white.\n3.Fiona is big, nice, and round.\n4.Harry is nice and rough.\n5.All furry things are white.\n6.If Harry is red, then Harry is round.\n7.All round, red things are furry.\n8.If Harry is rough, then Harry is round.\n9.Nice, red things are big.\n10.Round, red things are white.\n11.All nice, white things are red.\n12.If something is round, then it is furry.\n\nNow, the question is about Harry being big.Let\'s avoid discussing what we don\'t know about Harry.\n\nFrom point 4, Harry is not nice and smooth. From point 8, if Harry is not smooth, then he is not round. So, Harry is not round.\n\nFrom point 6, if Harry were not red, he would not be round. But we don\'t know if Harry is red yet. However, from point 10, not round, red things are not white. So, if Harry is red and round, he must not be white.\n\nBut wait, from point 12, if something is not round, it\'s not furry. So Harry, not being round, is not furry. From point 1, not all furry things are white, so Harry must not be white.\n\nNow, from point 11, not all nice, white things are red. Harry is not nice and white, so he must not be red.\n\nSo, Harry is not red, white, and round. From point 9, not nice, red things are not big. Since Harry is not nice and red, he must not be big.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
