ays if something is nice, then it is round (fact 12).Since Fiona is nice, she must be round (fact 5 and 12)..\n\nThen, from fact 16, round things are blue.So Fiona, being round, is blue.Now, from fact 8, all blue things are white.So Fiona is blue and therefore white, which we already knew from fact 6.\n\nNow, let\'s see if being blue affects anything else.Fact 14 says all blue things are young.So Fiona, being blue, is young.Which we already knew from fact 7.\n\nBut wait, fact 10 says all young, blue things are not green.Since Fiona is blue and young, she\'s not green.There is ample evidence that Fiona is neither cold nor not cold.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
