and the tiger likes the dog, then the dog does not like the squirrel.\n17.If something is round, then it eats the cat.\n18.If something needs the dog and it does not eat the tiger, then it is blue.\n19.If the dog is round, then the dog eats the squirrel.\n20.If something likes the tiger and it is kind, then the tiger likes the cat.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the cat eats the cat.Let\'s see if any of these statements directly or indirectly lead to that conclusion.\nNot considering any contradictions. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
