messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is big. Bob is cold. Bob is furry. Bob is smart. Fiona is cold. Fiona is not green. Fiona is white. Gary is smart. Harry is big. Harry is cold. Harry is smart. All green people are furry. If Gary is furry and Gary is not smart then Gary is white. Smart people are green. If Bob is not green and Bob is not white then Bob is furry. Big people are cold. If someone is smart and furry then they are big. If someone is white and not cold then they are not blue. All cold people are not blue.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Gary is cold.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "Gary is cold" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Bob is big, cold, furry, and smart.\n2.Fiona is cold, not green, and white.\n3.Gary is smart.\n4.Harry is big, cold, and smart.\n5.All green people are furry.\n6.If Gary is furry and not smart, then Gary is white.\n7.Smart people are green.\n8.If Bob is not green and not white, then Bob is furry.\n9.Big people are cold.\n10.If someone is smart and furry, then they are big.\n11.If someone is white and not cold, then they are not blue.\n12.All cold people are not blue.\n\nNow, the question is about Gary being cold.Let\'s see what we can deduce.\n\nFrom point 3, Gary is smart.From point 7, smart people are green.So Gary must be green.\n\nFrom point 6, if Gary is furry and not smart, then Gary is white.But Gary is smart, so the condition "Gary is not smart" is false.Therefore, the implication is always true regardless of whether Gary is furry or not.So this doesn\'t give us any new information about Gary\'s furiness.\n\nFrom point 10, if someone is smart and furry, then they are big.Since Gary is smart, if he\'s also furry, he must be big.But from point 3, we don\'t know if Gary is furry yet.However, from point 6, if Gary were furry and not smart, he\'d be white, but he\'s smart, so that doesn\'t affect him.So Gary could be furry or not, but if he is, he must be big.\n\nFrom point 4, Harry is big, cold, and smart.From point 9, big people are cold, which aligns with Harry being cold.\n\nNow, let\'s look at point 12: All cold people are not blue.So if someone is cold, they can\'t be blue.\n\nFrom point 11: If someone is white and not cold, then they are not blue.So white people who are not cold are not blue.But Fiona is white and cold, so that doesn\'t affect her color.However, if someone is white and not cold, they can\'t be blue.\n\nNow, back to Gary.We know he\'s smart and possibly furry.If he\'s furry, then from point 10, he\'s big.But we don\'t know if he\'s furry yet.\n\nWait, let\'s check point 8: If Bob is not green and not white, then Bob is furry.Bob is big, cold, furry, and smart.From point 7, Bob is green because he\'s smart.So Bob is green, so the condition "Bob is not green and not white" is false because he\'s green.Therefore, the implication doesn\'t tell us anything new about Bob\'s furiness, which we already know he is furry.\n\nNow, let\'s see if there\'s any information about Gary\'s furiness.From point 6, if Gary is furry and not smart, he\'s white.But Gary is smart, so the condition is false, so the implication doesn\'t affect him.So Gary could be furry or not, but if he is, he must be big.\n\nBut from point 10, if Gary is smart and furry, he\'s big.So if Gary is big, he\'s cold because from point 9, big people are cold.So if Gary is big, he\'s cold.But we don\'t know if Gary is big yet.\n\nWait, let\'s see if Gary is big.From point 10, if Gary is smart and furry, he\'s big.But we don\'t know if he\'s furry.Alternatively, from point 4, Harry is big, cold, and smart.So big people are cold, so if Gary is big, he\'s cold.But do we know if Gary is big?.\n\nAlternatively, let\'s think about point 12: All cold people are not blue.So if Gary is cold, he\'s not blue.But that doesn\'t tell us if he\'s cold or not.\n\nWait, let\'s see if there\'s any other clues.From point 6, if Gary is furry and not smart, he\'s white.But Gary is smart, so that doesn\'t help.So Gary could be furry or not.\n\nBut from point 10, if Gary is smart and furry, he\'s big.So if he\'s big, he\'s cold.But if he\'s not big, maybe he\'s not cold?Wait, no, because point 9 says big people are cold, but it doesn\'t say that only big people are cold.So maybe there are cold people who are not big.\nTherefore, Gary must NOT be cold\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 54%|#####3    | 323/600 [52:01<03:43,  1.24it/s]
