rel itself doesn't visit the squirrel unless there's a rule that causes it to do so. There's no such rule given.\n\nSo, the squirrel likes the cow, but we don't know if it likes the cat. Therefore, the answer is unknown.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought maybe the cat is chasing the lion, which is chasing the cow, but that doesn't directly link to the squirrel.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the cat is cold (2), but that's unrelated.\n\nSo, I think the answer is unknown, which is option C.\n</think>\n\nThe squirrel likes the cow, but there's no information linking the squirrel to liking the cat. Therefore, the statement is unknown.\n\nAnswer: C) Unknown",
