f she\'s smart, she must be green, but she\'s white.So that would mean she can\'t be smart because if she were, she\'d have to be green, which she isn\'t.\n\nAlternatively, maybe she\'s not smart.Let\'s see if there\'s any other way she could be smart without being green.Let\'s look at other points.\n\nPoint 9: All quiet, red people are smart.So, if someone is quiet and red, they are smart.Erin is not smart because she is white, not green.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
