ugh? Not directly. We know Gary is rough, but Gary is a different person. So, Harry could be rough or not.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Harry isn't rough. If Harry isn't rough, then from point 13, he's not kind. But from point 12, rough, kind people are quiet, but if Harry isn't rough, he could still be kind or not. Wait, no, point 13 says that if someone is young and rough, then they're kind. It doesn't say anything about young people who aren't rough.\n\nSo, Harry could be rough or not. If he's rough, then he's kind and quiet, making him round. If he's not rough, then we don't know if he's kind or not. But from point 14, only if he's quiet and furry, he's round. So, if he's not rough, we don't know if he's quiet.\n\nWait, but from point 10, all quiet, kind people are furry. So, if Harry is quiet and kind, he's furry, which he already is. But that doesn't necessarily mean he's quiet.\n\nAlternatively, maybe Harry isn't kind. If Harry isn't rough, he might not be kind either. But then, from point 14, if he's quiet and furry, he's round. But we don't know if he's quiet.\n\nWait, maybe there's another way. Since all big people are furry (point 8), and all young people are furry (point 9), and Harry is young, so Harry is furry. So, Harry is furry.\n\nNow, from point 15, furry people are rough. So, Harry is rough.\n\nWait, point 15 says all furry people are rough. So, since Harry is furry, he must be rough.\n\nThen, from point 12, rough, kind people are quiet. So, Harry is rough, so he must be kind. Then, from point 12, rough, kind people are quiet, so Harry is quiet.\n\nThen, from point 14, all quiet, furry people are round. So, Harry is quiet and furry, so he's round.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought point 15 says all furry people are rough, so Harry is rough. Then, from point 12, rough, kind people are quiet. So, Harry is rough, so he must be kind. Then, from point 12, rough, kind people are quiet, so Harry is quiet. Then, from point 14, Harry is quiet and furry, so he's round.\n\nSo, putting it all together:\n\n- Harry is young (point 7).\n- All young people are furry (point 9), so Harry is furry.\n- All furry people are rough (point 15), so Harry is rough.\n- Rough, kind people are quiet (point 12). Since Harry is rough, he must be kind.\n- Therefore, Harry is kind.\n- From point 12, rough, kind people are quiet, so Harry is quiet.\n- From point 14, all quiet, furry people are round. Harry is quiet and furry, so he's round.\n\nSo, Harry is round. Therefore, the statement is true.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Harry is round\" is true based on the logical deductions from the given premises.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
