messages:   63%|######2   | 376/600 [1:00:29<03:12,  1.17it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is kind. Anne is quiet. Anne is smart. Bob is kind. Bob is nice. Bob is smart. Fiona is not nice. Fiona is red. Gary is nice. Gary is white. If Bob is kind then Bob is smart. If something is kind and nice then it is smart. If something is nice and red then it is smart. If something is quiet and not nice then it is smart. All green things are kind. If Anne is quiet and Anne is white then Anne is kind. If Fiona is not nice then Fiona is green. All smart, kind things are white. If something is kind and green then it is quiet.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is smart.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out whether Fiona is smart based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll list out all the facts provided:.\n\n1.Anne is kind, quiet, and smart.\n2.Bob is kind, nice, and smart.\n3.Fiona is not nice and is red.\n4.Gary is nice and white.\n5.If Bob is kind, then Bob is smart.(Which we already know since Bob is kind and smart.).\n6.If something is kind and nice, then it is smart.(So, any kind and nice thing is smart.).\n7.If something is nice and red, then it is smart.(Fiona is nice and red, so according to this rule, Fiona should be smart.).\n8.If something is quiet and not nice, then it is smart.(Anne is quiet and not nice, so she's smart, which we already know.).\n9.All green things are kind.(Not directly relevant to Fiona, but good to note.).\n10.If Anne is quiet and white, then she is kind.(Anne is quiet and white, so she's kind, which we know.).\n11.If Fiona is not nice, then Fiona is green.(Fiona is not nice, so she should be green.But Fiona is red, so there's a conflict here.).\n12.All smart, kind things are white.(So, if something is smart and kind, it's white.But Fiona is red, so maybe she's not smart and kind.If Fiona were not nice and green, she'd be smart, but Fiona is red, so this doesn't apply.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
