formation.Statement 13 says smooth, square things are small, which we\'ve already used.Statement 17 says black things are square, which Gary is not, so that\'s consistent.Statement 18 says if Dave is warm, he\'s black, but that doesn\'t affect Gary.Statement 19 is about black, old things being mean, which again doesn\'t impact Gary\'s warmth.\n\nSo, putting it together: Gary is square (4), which makes him small (12), which makes him warm (11), which makes him smooth (14).So yes, Gary is warm.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions or missing links here\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
