messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe cow is young. The cow sees the lion. The dog likes the cow. The dog likes the rabbit. The dog sees the rabbit. The lion is young. The lion sees the cow. The lion sees the dog. The lion sees the rabbit. The rabbit is round. The rabbit likes the cow. If someone visits the rabbit then the rabbit likes the lion. If someone likes the rabbit and the rabbit is red then the rabbit is big. If someone likes the lion and they see the rabbit then the lion likes the rabbit. If someone is young then they like the rabbit. If someone is young then they see the lion. If the lion is big then the lion visits the dog. If the rabbit likes the lion then the rabbit is young. If someone is young and they like the rabbit then they visit the rabbit.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The rabbit does not see the lion.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to figure out whether the statement "The rabbit does not see the lion" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.Let me go through the information step by step.\n\nFirst, I\'ll list out all the given statements to make it easier to reference:.\n\n1.The cow is young.\n2.The cow sees the lion.\n3.The dog likes the cow.\n4.The dog likes the rabbit.\n5.The dog sees the rabbit.\n6.The lion is young.\n7.The lion sees the cow.\n8.The lion sees the dog.\n9.The lion sees the rabbit.\n10.The rabbit is round.\n11.The rabbit likes the cow.\n12.If someone visits the rabbit, then the rabbit likes the lion.\n13.If someone likes the rabbit and the rabbit is red, then the rabbit is big.\n14.If someone likes the lion and they see the rabbit, then the lion likes the rabbit.\n15.If someone is young, then they like the rabbit.\n16.If someone is young, then they see the lion.\n17.If the lion is big, then the lion visits the dog.\n18.If the rabbit likes the lion, then the rabbit is young.\n19.If someone is young and they like the rabbit, then they visit the rabbit.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the rabbit does not see the lion.So, I need to determine if the rabbit sees the lion or not based on these statements.\n\nLooking at statement 9: The lion sees the rabbit.So, the lion sees the rabbit.But does that mean the rabbit sees the lion?Not necessarily.Because seeing is not necessarily mutual.So, just because the lion sees the rabbit doesn\'t mean the rabbit sees the lion.\n\nBut let\'s check if there\'s any information about the rabbit seeing the lion.Statement 18 says: If the rabbit likes the lion, then the rabbit is young.So, if the rabbit likes the lion, then the rabbit must be young.But does that help us?Not directly, because we don\'t know if the rabbit likes the lion.\n\nStatement 14: If someone likes the lion and they see the rabbit, then the lion likes the rabbit.So, if the rabbit sees the lion, then the lion likes the rabbit.But we don\'t know if the rabbit sees the lion yet.\n\nStatement 19: If someone is young and they like the rabbit, then they visit the rabbit.So, if someone (maybe the cow or the lion) likes the rabbit and is young, they visit it.But again, we don\'t know if the rabbit likes the lion.\n\nWait, let\'s think about the rabbit\'s perspective.The rabbit likes the cow (statement 11).The rabbit is round (10).The rabbit is liked by the dog (4 and 11).The dog sees the rabbit (5).The dog likes the rabbit (4).The dog likes the cow (3).The cow is young (1) and sees the lion (2).The cow likes the rabbit (11).The lion is young (6) and likes the cow (7), the dog (8), and the rabbit (9).The lion sees the cow (7), the dog (8), and the rabbit (9).The rabbit is round (10), likes the cow (11), and if someone likes the rabbit and it\'s red, it\'s big (13).But we don\'t know if the rabbit is red or not.The rabbit sees the lion, which means the rabbit does not like the lion.Therefore, it\'s confirmed that the rabbit is old.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 67%|######6   | 400/600 [1:03:02<02:13,  1.50it/s] 67%|######6   | 401/600 [1:03:02<01:50,  1.79it/s]
