n.But since all blue people are cold, then all blue people are green.So Charlie, being blue, must be green.But that contradicts him being blue.So perhaps the rules are conflicting, but that\'s unlikely.Maybe I\'m misapplying the rules.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps rule 15 is trying to say that blue people are green if they\'re cold, but that\'s not necessarily the case.Maybe it\'s a conditional statement.So if someone is blue and cold, then they are green.But since all blue people are cold, then all blue people must be green.So Charlie, being blue, must be green.But that contradicts him being blue.So perhaps the rules are conflicting, but that\'s unlikely.Maybe I\'m misapplying the rules.\n\nWait, maybe I\'m overcomplicating this.Let\'s try to focus on Charlie\'s attributes.\n\nCharlie is blue and quiet.From rule 17: If Charlie is not quiet, then he is not round.But Charlie is quiet, so rule 17 doesn\'t apply.So we don\'t know if Charlie is round or not based on that.\n\nRule 18: If Gary is blue and round, then Gary is not cold.But Gary is green, so he\'s not blue, so rule 18 doesn\'t apply to him.\n\nRule 19: All round people are not furry.So if Charlie is round, he\'s not furry.But we don\'t know if he\'s round yet.\n\nRule 20: If someone is cold and not furry, then they are white.So if Charlie is cold and not furry, then he\'s white.But we don\'t know if he\'s cold or not.\n\nWait, from rule 16: All blue people are cold.So Charlie, being blue, is cold.So Charlie is cold.\n\nFrom rule 20: If someone is cold and not furry, then they are white.So if Charlie is cold and not furry, he\'s white.But we don\'t know if he\'s furry.\n\nFrom rule 19: All round people are not furry.So if Charlie is round, he\'s not furry.But we don\'t know if he\'s round.\n\nSo let\'s see: Charlie is blue and quiet.He\'s cold (from rule 16).If he\'s round, then he\'s not furry (rule 19).If he\'s not round, then we don\'t know about being furry.\n\nBut from rule 13: If someone is blue and not qu