se is not smooth (statement 7).So the question is whether the bald eagle is not smooth.\n\nBut smoothness is not a property of the mouse, necessarily of the bald eagle.The context mentions something about the bald eagle being smooth or not.It only mentions that the mouse is not smooth.So there\'s information linking the bald eagle\'s smoothness to something else.\n\nWait, but maybe there\'s no connection through the mouse.If the mouse is not smooth, and the mouse visits the bald eagle, does that mean the bald eagle is not smooth?No, because smoothness is not a property of the mouse, not the eagle.Unless there\'s a rule that if something is not smooth, then the thing it visits is not smooth, but I see such a rule in the given statements.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bald eagle\'s smoothness is not inferred from the mouse\'s smoothness, but that\'s stated.The context provides information about the bald eagle\'s smoothness.So based on the given information, we can determine whether the bald eagle is not smooth or not\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 88%|########8 | 529/600 [1:12:06<02:19,  1.96s/it]
