ement 11 says if someone is hot and dislikes the spotted owl, they like the bird.So, if the hot spotted owl dislikes the spotted owl, then it would like the bird.But does the hot spotted owl dislike the spotted owl?There\'s no information about that.So, we can\'t conclude that.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the hot spotted owl dislikes the cat (from 17), but that doesn\'t necessarily mean it dislikes the spotted owl.\n\nSo, putting it all together, we have the spotted owl dislikes the cat (1), and the hot spotted owl is established (17).But there\'s no direct or indirect evidence that the hot spotted owl dislikes the spotted owl, which would allow it to like the bird (statement 11).Therefore, we can\'t conclude that the spotted owl dislikes the bird.\n\nWait, but statement 10 says the rat dislikes the spotted owl.So, the rat dislikes the spotted owl, but that\'s the rat, not the spotted owl.So, the spotted owl doesn\'t necessarily dislike itself\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
