the bear is round because the lion needs both the bear and itself, making the bear round (statement 11). But being round doesn't necessarily mean it needs the lion. It just means it is round.\n\nBut from statement 10, the bear does not see the bald eagle, so it does not need the lion. Therefore, the bear does not need the lion.\n\nSo, the answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe bear does not need the lion.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
